  "filled_passage": "### A\n\nMy aunt runs a bakery (1) which opens at seven every morning. Yesterday she put three small (2) cakes (cake) in the window. They were (3) cheaper (cheap) than the large cakes on the shelf. I wrote their prices as (4) clearly (clear) as I could. Before leaving, I checked that each price was beside the correct cake.\n\n### B\n\nOur art teacher brought an old painting to class. The colours were (5) brighter (bright) than I had expected. She told us (6) to look at the shadows before mixing our paints. I had always been afraid (7) of making mistakes, but she explained that we could let the paper dry and try again on another sheet.\n\n### C\n\nAt the station we saw a passenger (8) pushing (push) a red bicycle towards the lift. He was the man (9) whose ticket my brother had found on a bench. We returned it to him before the train arrived. He thanked us for (10) returning (return) it. We were glad that a small discovery had solved his problem.",
